In plain words (this summary is not the licence; the terms below are):

  - Anyone may use OpenWX, free of charge. That includes businesses, small studios,
    and pages or channels that make money from the weather coverage they produce.
  - Anyone may change it, build on it and share it.
  - Anything you share that is based on OpenWX keeps this same licence, with its
    source code.
  - Making money from the software itself (selling it, charging for access to it,
    bundling it into a paid product, or reselling it as a hosted service) needs a
    Commercial Waiver: a donation of US $500 or more to the project grants one.
  - Third-party parts (radar services, music, fonts, icons, libraries) keep their
    own licences.
  - There is no warranty, and the authors are not liable for what happens when you
    use it. OpenWX is not an official warning source.
