1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means the copyright holder(s) of the Software, acting through the
maintainers of the OpenWX Broadcasting project at the address above.

"Software" means the source code, object code, documentation and other original
works of authorship that the Licensor makes available under this Licence,
including OpenWX Broadcasting, OpenWX Relay and the `openwx` tool. It does not
include Third-Party Components.

"Third-Party Components" means any work included with or used by the Software
that is under a different licence or terms, including libraries, fonts, icons,
music, map and boundary data, and online data services. Each is listed or
identified in `docs/licensing.md`, its own folder, or its own licence file.

"Derivative Work" means any work that is based on, modified from, or contains
all or a substantial part of the Software.

"Distribute" means to give, sell, publish or otherwise make a copy of the
Software or a Derivative Work available to anyone else. Letting people use a
Derivative Work over a network (for example, as a hosted service or a hosted
relay) also counts as Distributing it.

"You" means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this Licence.

"Commercial Use" means making money from the Software or a Derivative Work
itself: selling, renting or licensing it, charging for access to it or for
copies of it, bundling it with a paid product or service, or offering it to
others as a paid hosted service.

"Production Use" means using the Software to make weather coverage, graphics,
shows, posts or other output, by anyone, including businesses, broadcasters,
studios, and pages or channels that earn money from advertising, sponsorship,
subscriptions or paying clients. Production Use is not Commercial Use, and what
You make with the Software is Yours.

"Source Code" means the preferred form of a work for making changes to it,
including the build scripts needed to produce a working program.

