4. COMMERCIAL USE AND THE COMMERCIAL WAIVER

  (a) Commercial Use is not permitted without a Commercial Waiver, whether or not
      the Source Code is shared. Production Use never needs one.

  (b) A Commercial Waiver is granted to an individual or legal entity that makes a
      single donation of US $500 or more to the OpenWX Broadcasting project
      through a donation channel the Licensor lists in the project repository,
      and receives written confirmation (including by e-mail or a published
      sponsor listing) from the Licensor.

  (c) A Commercial Waiver lets the holder use, modify and Distribute the Software
      and its Derivative Works for Commercial Use, without the conditions in
      section 3(a) and 3(c). Sections 3(b), 3(e), 5, 6, 7 and 8 still apply.

  (d) A Commercial Waiver is perpetual for every version of the Software
      released before or within one year after the date of the donation. It
      applies to the donor and to entities it controls. It may not be
      sold, sublicensed or transferred, except with the sale of the whole business
      that holds it.

  (e) The Licensor may set a different donation amount for versions released
      after a future change to this Licence. Waivers already granted are not
      affected.


